Logic hai — recursively traverse karte hain deeply nested structure, RecursionError reproduce karte hain, phir explicit stack ke saath iterative approach mein convert karte hain aur verify karte hain.

Pehle Python script chalata hoon jo recursive traversal fail karega:

```python
# Recursive tree traversal - depth 5000+ will blow recursion limit (~1000)
# Simulating a deeply nested chain structure
class Node:
    def __init__(self, value, children=None):
        self.value = value
        self.children = children or []

def build_deep_chain(depth):
    """Create a chain of nodes depth levels deep"""
    node = Node(f"leaf_{depth}")
    for i in range(depth-1, 0, -1):
        node = Node(f"node_{i}", [node])
    return node

def recursive_traversal(node, depth=0):
    """Recursively visit all nodes (will fail for depth > recursion limit)"""
    print(f"Depth {depth}: {node.value}", end=" -> " if node.children else "\n")
    for child in node.children:
        recursive_traversal(child, depth+1)

print("Building deep chain with depth 5000...")
root = build_deep_chain(5000)
print("Attempting recursive traversal...")
try:
    recursive_traversal(root)
except RecursionError as e:
    print(f"\nRecursionError caught: {e}")
```

